","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":6031,"open_issues":634,"watchers":21911,"default_branch":"release-v2","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"@ojw28 , I am trying to implement your new track switching system.\r\nIt doesn't behave logically.\r\n1. I turn on the track:\r\nMediaItem mediaItem = MediaItem.fromUri(Uri.parse(path));\r\n                if (position > 0)\r\n                    mMediaPlayer.setMediaItem(mediaItem, position);\r\n                else\r\n                    mMediaPlayer.setMediaItem(mediaItem, true);\r\n                mMediaPlayer.prepare();\r\n2. I am waiting: Player.STATE_READY  and do mMediaPlayer.clearMediaItems();\r\n3. Then I turn on the next track at once:\r\nMediaItem mediaItem = MediaItem.fromUri(Uri.parse(path));\r\n                if (position > 0)\r\n                    mMediaPlayer.setMediaItem(mediaItem, position);\r\n                else\r\n                    mMediaPlayer.setMediaItem(mediaItem, true);\r\n                mMediaPlayer.prepare();\r\n4. The Player.STATE_ENDED event is triggered. Why? The first track was not finished. The second track has not started playing yet.\r\n5. The Player.STATE_READY event is not triggered. How do I know that the player has finished onPrepare?\r\n\r\nI think the implementation of the new playlist system will be delayed...\r\nThere are many questions.\r\nAnd I think most people will not use this functionality. Everyone needs to play one file. The playlist is a part of the application, not the playback module (ExoPlayer).\r\n\r\nThe problem does not appear if I use the old method:\r\nmMediaPlayer.prepare(progressiveSource.createMediaSource(new MediaItem.Builder().setUri(Uri.parse(path)).build()), !haveStartPosition, false);","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8192/reactions","total_c